message: "If you use this result or these tools, please cite them as below."
title: "Moki & Julio: Ueda's oscillator is chaotic - a computer-assisted proof"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23172757"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/ueda-chaos"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - Ueda attractor
  - Duffing equation
  - forced oscillator
  - chaos
  - symbolic dynamics
  - topological entropy
  - covering relations
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - CAPD
abstract: >-
  Ueda's forced cubic oscillator x'' + 0.05 x' + x^3 = 7.5 cos t, the case Ueda calls his 'representative' chaotic
  attractor, has been called chaotic on numerical evidence only. We prove, with rigorous interval-arithmetic integration
  (CAPD), covering relations A => A, A => C0 => C1 => C2 => C3 => A for its time-2pi map on five disjoint sets built
  around the saddle fixed point D and a numerically computed homoclinic loop. Consequently every itinerary of
  one-period stays near D and five-period excursions is realised by a true solution, there are infinitely many periodic
  orbits, and the topological entropy of the map is at least ln of the plastic number (about 0.2812 per period). The
  claim concerns a chaotic invariant set, not the whole observed attractor. Two
  independently written checkers, positive and negative controls and a one-command reproduction are included.
